.TH SDL_DestroyRWLock 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_DestroyRWLock \- Destroy a read/write lock created with
.BR SDL_CreateRWLock ().

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_mutex.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_DestroyRWLock(SDL_RWLock *rwlock);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function must be called on any read/write lock that is no longer needed\[char46] Failure to destroy a rwlock will result in a system memory or resource leak\[char46] While it is safe to destroy a rwlock that is _unlocked_, it is not safe to attempt to destroy a locked rwlock, and may result in undefined behavior depending on the platform\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I rwlock
the rwlock to destroy\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateRWLock (3)
